[% PROCESS util.tt -%]
<div class="row">
  <div class="col-md-12">
    <h1 class="section-title">About Perl School</h1>

    <p class="lead">Perl School is an independent publisher specialising
      in books for the Perl community.</p>

    <p>Traditional technical publishers have largely moved away from Perl.
      We haven't.</p>

    <p>There is still useful Perl knowledge worth writing down and sharing,
      even when the potential audience is too small to interest a large
      publisher. Perl School exists to publish those books.</p>

    <p>We publish practical books by experienced Perl developers, from broad
      introductions to highly specialised subjects. We don't need every book
      to be a bestseller. A book that is useful to a few hundred Perl
      programmers can still be well worth publishing.</p>

    <h2 class="section-title">Publishing Perl books</h2>

    <p>Perl School works with authors to turn their knowledge into books
      without making the process unnecessarily complicated. We help with
      editing and production, create ebook and print editions, and handle
      publication and distribution.</p>

    <p>Our books are available electronically, and new titles are generally
      also published as print-on-demand paperbacks. That lets us produce
      specialist printed books without needing warehouses, print runs or
      boxes of unsold stock.</p>

    <p>We're particularly interested in books that might struggle to find
      a home with a traditional publisher. That could mean a book about a
      particular Perl module or framework, a specialist area of Perl
      development, or a new edition of an older Perl book whose rights have
      returned to its author.</p>

    <h2 class="section-title">A little history</h2>

    <p>Perl School was created by Dave Cross in 2012 as a series of
      low-cost weekend Perl training courses. In 2017 the name was revived
      for a new publishing project, beginning with
      <a href="/books/perl-taster/"><i>Perl Taster</i></a>.</p>

    <p>Since then Perl School has grown into a small independent publisher,
      with <a href="/books/">books by several authors</a> covering a growing
      range of Perl subjects.</p>

    <h2 class="section-title">About Dave Cross</h2>

    <figure class="bio-figure">
      [% an_image('dave', 'Dave Cross', 'bio-photo img-fluid', 'png') -%]
      <figcaption class="bio-caption muted">
        Dave Cross - founder of Perl School.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <p>Dave Cross is a Perl developer, author and trainer who has been part
      of the Perl community since the 1990s. He is the author of
      <i>Data Munging with Perl</i> and co-author of
      <i>Perl Template Toolkit</i>, and has spoken and taught at Perl and
      open source conferences for many years.</p>

    <p>He founded London Perl Mongers in 1998 and received a White Camel
      Award in 2004 for his contributions to the Perl community. Perl School
      is published by his company, Magnum Solutions Ltd.</p>

    <div class="clearfix"></div>

    <aside class="callout mt-4">
      <p class="mb-2"><strong>Know something about Perl that deserves a
        book?</strong></p>
      <p class="mb-0">
        We're always interested in hearing from potential authors.
        <a href="/write-for-us/">Find out about writing for Perl School</a>.
      </p>
    </aside>
  </div>
</div>
